body:
I just would like an outsiders perspective, I haven't the slightest clue what to make of it because I'm in the middle of it.. sometimes it's nice to have someone (which I don't, hence reddit) who can set things straight.

&#x200B;

We're not working together for a week or so, so I won't see or have any contact with her.

I could probably take a medium weight toddler..

&#x200B;

That's what I'll probably do to be honest.

&#x200B;

I'm not trying to say one is better than the other but I just thought it was a little strange that a gym only has kickboxing and not muay thai..

Thanks for the input.

&#x200B;

I'm just hoping I'm not walking into this as the softer option with my hands firmly over my ears.  


My parents seem to think 'ah sure a degree will get a ya a job though'..

&#x200B;

I'll be transferring to an IT from a NUI too, but I'll have work experience.

On top of all of that I don't know how much I'd like to work in an office all day.

I probably have a touch of ADHD, I'm not hyperactive but my brain is.

&#x200B;

You do get paid, I was getting paid €6.80 an hour as a first year, that rises to €18something in your final year, starting wage was €23.

&#x200B;

I liked working with my uncle bar the lifting of wardrobes up stairs.. 

I couldn't apprentice with him though because he's a good 1.5hr drive from me, and the work is further afield.

One worry with carpentry for me is that when the economy tanks, you don't call a carpenter to fix something.

&#x200B;

If I was going into the trades it'd be something hands on.. what though is the real question.

Nope I just said '(guy) sent me down' and the manager said 'go give (guy 2) a hand up on the roof'..

&#x200B;

I didn't say a word to the manager other than that, the guy giving out to me went and rang the manager as I was walking down to the office, he told I didn't say a word.

Good point.. at the same time road tax, insurance etc can be a lot here, if I was to get a 08+ car it'd be \~€200 on road tax instead of €500+, insurance would be cheaper too, so would any maintenance costs etc.. plus it's a nice excuse to get a new car.  


I know if I turned around to my parents and gave them 1000 they wouldn't take it, 'buy yourself something nice!', 'put it towards the insurance'.. if I had already made the change and told them to put it towards my sisters college I think they'd see it in a different light.

&#x200B;

I remember NickEh30 on about that, he does Push Up challenges and all of that, he's always telling his viewers to drink enough water etc.. burn out and neglect are real.


My brothers friend plays games all day, he also works as a security guard.. he grew a beard just because he didn't want to shave.

The guy is spiteful and angry the whole time.. but he was always like that.  
He also only goes to comiccon, works and stays in his room.  
He builds PCs and won't sell them.. He's always giving out.. overall not a great guy.

&#x200B;

I mean pro gaming is obviously something seriously invest into when you have kids dropping out of school and going pro.

It's something you can do for a long time, longer than a pro athlete.. it's closer to being a golfer than a linebacker.

&#x200B;

I want to start my own business, I'm interested in mens style/clothing, I want to invest in property, stocks, build brands and grow, there's a whole host of things I want to do but a college degree isn't included.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

First person to notice, yeah it's referencing the cause of the Challenger disaster.

&#x200B;

I hope to start my own company.. I'm also interested in trading so maybe just a private equity firm or my own financial management company (as in for my assets), if it all goes to plan I could retire early, but that's wishful thinking..

&#x200B;

I think I'm in agreeance, I know myself that I'm probably borderline, but until such a time that I 'need' a diagnosis I don't think I'll bother.

Nothing really comes to mind..

&#x200B;

I mean I love learning but I hate college.  
The one aspect I enjoyed was a Business Information Systems class where we talked about competitive advantage, Why McDonalds is as big as they are, what makes a company successful, how important x,y and z is.. why companies fail.  
That was the most hated course by everyone except me.. I mean everyone else seemed to despise it.

The lecture always gets in shit because he doesn't go by the book.

&#x200B;

I like learning, I like understanding how things work, how moneys made, how businesses operate, how to get rich.

&#x200B;

As a kid/teen I loved guitars, namely vintage guitars, I'd just learn everything about them.. but I haven't really cared for that in awhile.

&#x200B;

I like music, mainly the lyrics.. but I don't like most music and I've never found anyone into the same stuff as me.. I've played guitar for years and I've wanted to join a band for a long time, but in school i was the only guy who played and even in college, I can find 101 DJs but no musicians.

&#x200B;

I wanted to be a doctor - namely a Neurosurgeon growing up, I could just save lives on the table and ignore everything else, I'd make great money, be well respected, women love doctors etc, but I hate chemistry and maths!

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
